"VRCE-5-34-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":12,"english":"And if Kākutstha lives untouched by ill, then why does he not burn the earth, encircled by the ocean with his ire like to the fire of dissolution?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"12bf8737cf6406eabbdab10a70c095c14a92ddfa4fe7c7688de73b2cbadef342","compact":"32c27bd73e03b0902938f60d3161fa8bb2681f5118b695970201b1b34061a2e4","nasal":"95b25e5d02daae5a362c6e894a69b4f418230e529517f8adc2d214032edf7ebd"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":13,"english":"Or they are capable of discomfiting the celestials in a battle but me-thinks by my illluck, the end of my miseries has not arrived as yet.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9260803bc8e2366378533f5d8d9141990849e438c6463d74bcd9496082b1c52a","compact":"b6c48c7660fcacafea11a94296234ee6ece3476529f193d22993396f433e2076","nasal":"7979416e364973e664fe2a600d8c195d700277083774cf4a6bd5675ba549283b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":14,"english":"Is Rāma greatly pained? Does he grieve? Is that foremost of men making preparations of my rescue?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fcb0c71017ae0b8ae5c745d82cb99c0d8b21fe23ad064d21bdbf2ff31d4a9a5a","compact":"40a1484487c41559f3b95c0d70caff068f7419d1ff4788f0e98