"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c012e3dda3e1d0a6b89da3b0172e803caa418cd8ae72081dee94e126db738a65","compact":"ede1c3c0f2fabd67cc48fcb92e0cc2fcef58ad1f07ed9a1d6d3715282d289ecb","nasal":"ede1c3c0f2fabd67cc48fcb92e0cc2fcef58ad1f07ed9a1d6d3715282d289ecb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-27","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":27,"english":"Is not the gold-hued and lotus-smelling countenance (of Rāma) dried up my absence like to lotus dried up by the rays of the sun in shallow water?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aaeb22c28266a942cb6334fdc4bb9010608ba9ead5292160451219137ce95453","compact":"0f900021bacbf739448ae8790ff57d0d565456ca7f48b7bbbb71a493e4a120ae","nasal":"18783c3b471d893091591d0c6783fb5a422f4210257ef280ab0e3874d4a26abe"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-28","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":28,"english":"Does he still hold patience in his heart, who, renouncing his kingdom for virtue and repairing, on foot with me even to the forest, was not stricken with fear and grief?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.462,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034028","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b2933c8a7086048b01fb75109f1b5830b5184cefc0658fd67fea739640591784","compact":"11d2fe0efd6f83eeb0063559fd9767d43f156c6680e1ac77979ddfdf3cb7ea6e","nasal":"11d2fe0efd6f83eeb0063559fd9767d43f156c6680e1ac77979ddfdf3cb7ea6e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-29","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":29,"english":"His love for his mother, father or any other person is not greater than or equal to his love for me. O messenger, I shall keep my life so long I do not hear anything about my dear one.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034029","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11d61727f1b98f0f7707b7c09f5a2f49c79df578d9ddd893bdd4a30e11f57b43","compact":"5b1b59cb359ac07c9eac9c1b0e4ffee9f400b3a73d75c1fb7708667fd463d932","nasal":"5b1b59cb359ac07c9eac9c1b0e4ffee9f400b3a73d75c1fb7708667fd463d932"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-30","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":30,"english":"Having addressed that lord of monkeys with these highly sound and sweet accents, that graceful and worshipful dame ceased, with a view to hear again from him pleasant tales regarding Rāma.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-29"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034030","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21a0e5b23a2f3e4d87735c0cf8e53dc5f3370c8966f633dabb21890d9616fa01","compact":"465fa21c4ddf92652c443e1d454eb84bf1ff48672e35194de4fc0166f39a5daa","nasal":"5f3c632858e229f39ee90dc9fbe661983698e22fb8af059cd4abf071ecd46413"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-31","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":31,"english":"Hearing the words of Sītā the terribly powerful Măruti, placing his joined palms on his head said,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-30"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034031","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1c37e20e8feb9ccc9bf559aabebcc4239f6990366a0a2015e1732fe84418060f","compact":"f9762fd79f38d261f390dc37c092947518263db37f95347fc5e2478a1b7d818f","nasal":"fe12f13609d436c6a89389b6e1f26d817c8970c873bd007eae1dee04c39313ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-32","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":32,"english":"The lotus-eyed Rāma dose not know that you are here, and hence he has not been able to rescue you like to Purandara regaining Saci. Hearing about you from me soon shall Rāghava come assisted by a large army of monkeys and bears.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.387,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-31","DUTT-5-36-32"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034032","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e809c15e30877d3d91705d92d71286adcb634619117ac746bfbe44c3ef920304","compact":"dd05b84071b6cc72d18fe5b4400be347ac494db054dcd8f734b125af28b02dbe","nasal":"dd05b84071b6cc72d18fe5b4400be347ac494db054dcd8f734b125af28b02dbe"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-33","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":33,"english":"Impeding the course of the unagitated deep and building by means of his terrible shafts, a bridge across it, Kākutstha, shall divest the city Lankā of all the Rākşasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.673,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-33"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034033","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9221bca0e06675195fa6844f7955f7137ddcf246cbf2a14fa026834210f79508","compact":"586e84b2ea15f79d76ed97bcc5cc0caea9076c2c3707a8cf177932ede013d928","nasal":"6cbd7d48d6c4bcd950a4c05c9ea4dc91bb4c28b30f76dd0eab8d662d404a3089"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-34","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":34,"english":"And forsooth shall Rāma destroy them, even if the celestials, or Death himself stand in his way.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-34"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034034","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"90a56396e8b6f707971cb8ddcf8fd24c36e50921da8972e05bd8c92c2ee33a9e","compact":"cae31172d80ded96cc782cf29d4b9f5abd6bb95b47033b47ec455f793d754df8","nasal":"3e20793159d61abf0b4eafc41fbb0c1e98330b8dcd29dfa53bf4350e7588e8f4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-35","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":35,"english":"O worshipful dame, stricken with grief in your absence, Rāma is restless like to an elephant smitten by a lion.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.727,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-35"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034035","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"afc24dbf8558466458a5e162bb65ad06f35fecee05be487e35214a0c92c46f16","compact":"4191f7890d27771103abf1b7bf769c649951684804cc1ae98d026bcb26e81963","nasal":"4191f7890d27771103abf1b7bf769c649951684804cc1ae98d026bcb26e81963"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-36","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":36,"english":"I can swear, O worshipful dame, by the mounts Mandara, Malaya, Vindhya, Sumeru, Dardura and all the fruits and roots, that you shall behold like to the rising of the full moon, the countenance of Rāma having beautiful eyes, graceful, Bimba-like lips and beautified with beautiful kundalas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.809,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034036","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e30d47269a3746c2277f0dc894d4de1a02705f052222dd35fab6367199fe4ca","compact":"7ecbfae7c5afc3e9cbd498a85dfce5ea739cf7f9ac26faf47ddae046f66e90a2","nasal":"9035ca9a926302f2857df95014bc1e20041837401e5f0e27ea77fedae3981894"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-37","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":37,"english":"I can swear, O worshipful dame, by the mounts Mandara, Malaya, Vindhya, Sumeru, Dardura and all the fruits and roots, that you shall behold like to the rising of the full moon, the countenance of Rāma having beautiful eyes, graceful, Bimba-like lips and beautified with beautiful kundalas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.884,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-36"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034037","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"651db0e067add810631d1e046b084a321d55d51a68fc461d7c5dd80bc6ca95b6","compact":"06ef3c6e2956b4c80d9b4ad5a74b904c9bfe1b4d72ac267a39b46a5397576ecf","nasal":"940adb50874f6b2a35aadf40026b1a29efa767827ee516057c6f7bccaa95b816"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-38","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":38,"english":"You shall soon behold, O Vaidehī, Rāma, on the mount Prasravana, like to the performer of hundred sacrifices seated on the back of the elephant (Airăvata).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-37"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034038","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2d801cb49d5abff9a6383122d467ebb37d38805fc93c1b228b47855baf1503e","compact":"fd25cd5ae543d671d6a839bccb5c4e9308e4620de6c4deb12c489dcffae7b1b4","nasal":"fd25cd5ae543d671d6a839bccb5c4e9308e4620de6c4deb12c489dcffae7b1b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-39","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":39,"english":"Rāghava dose not take meat nor drink honeyế he takes every day in the evening boiled rice and such wild fruits as are sanctioned by the Sastras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-38"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034039","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"033eb4ff668a6c1ff57138f611fe1152634ef6e7362bab13fb7aa90bbf5be2f2","compact":"d8058d5b2fdb094c63c3781dc9bafadd0c242b197613dc1df3f34eefc8ad8de4","nasal":"ade8487396aca94b2f8904017c53d2162bd8f133f1407f27b6d48dce3f34b3af"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-40","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":40,"english":"His heart is so much attached to you, that he does not drive away even flies, insects and snakes from his body.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.891,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-39"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034040","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"80c99501b8fd6c1b2e6bd87654cd7f1f778798ade56395d4b8ff71fca386994a","compact":"b127bd06cc7514e5d4bdf3a61bae70bbf643509e89923ffcfd0abfb30b2e5514","nasal":"6dcc9644805170acbb65df07eff7bd96b27c7867f9fca2a9709a7a559d793498"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-41","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":41,"english":"Rāma is always engaged in meditations, overwhelmed with grief, and he has no other thought but seeing you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-40"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034041","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a07f18389a8a1c77226e5dadf9d326c97250b096c9fe3c7bce02191c0fdfcf6","compact":"ee474f5968abbf187c14e34c8401a92094832499d94f397fef72d37a8eec598b","nasal":"f76baae11164ff5c061e48e22121cc41f188eaff11ae6a1eb1274ba2aaa820c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-34-42","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":34,"verse":42,"english":"Rāma has no sleep and even when asleep that best of men awakes exclaiming in sweep accents, 'O Sītā!'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-36-41"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5034042","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3d1f5ad699d